{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.GluingBridge","lean:module:QOU.Knot.GeneratedGluing"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.satisfiesEdgeEquations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.satisfiesEdgeEquations","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/SixOneCertified.lean#L114-L123","doc":"**`6₁` satisfies its edge gluing equations**, at every root of the shape field's\nminimal polynomial.\n\nThe generated identities now *certify a structure* rather than standing alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.gluing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.gluing","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/SixOneCertified.lean#L60-L65","doc":"`6₁`'s four edge equations as exponent data, from SnapPy's integer matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.triangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.SixOneCertified.triangulation","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/SixOneCertified.lean#L50-L58","doc":"The four `6₁` shapes as `Shape`s, at an arbitrary root of the minimal polynomial.\n\n`Shape.ne_one` is derived from the generated `one_sub_zⱼ_ne_zero`: `1 - z ≠ 0` and\n`z = 1` are contradictory. ","signatureChunk":0}]}